sentences.l:
Of son and of father,
kindly one, I pray, have pity; for you can do all things, nor you
in vain over the Avernian groves Hecate set;

if Orpheus could summon the shades of his wife,
relying on the Thracian lyre and tuneful strings,
if his brother Pollux by alternate death redeemed,
and goes and returns the road so often.

sentences.t:
Latet arbore opaca
aureus et foliis et lento vimine ramus,
Iunoni infernae dictus sacer;

sentences.l:
Lies hidden in a shady tree
a golden both in leaves and in pliant twig bough,
to Juno of the lower world called sacred;
